{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310562,"nonce":"ojXF+WBbSENUxfa/iZeD2FRbp1s=","title":"FIXED 63f45661: the conformance harness scored PASSING cases as NO_OUTPUT because `printf \\\"$out\\\" | grep -q` under `set -o pipefail` ...","message":"`set -uo pipefail` + `elif printf '%s' \"$out\" | grep -q '^CONFORMANCE_OK'`.\n`grep -q` exits at the FIRST match and closes the pipe; bash's printf writes a line\nat a time; the next write takes SIGPIPE; pipefail adopts 141 as the pipeline status.\n**The condition is false BECAUSE the match succeeded early.** A passing test prints\n`CONFORMANCE_OK` on line 1, so the more it printed after that, the likelier its own\nsuccess suppressed the check.\n\nCI-only because `RAYZOR_TIER_TRACE_STARTUP=1` (conformance.yml) adds ~34 lines after\nline 1; a local run has none and printf finishes first. Measured at CI scale\n(5000-line tail): pipe form missed **50/50**, file form **0/50**.\n\nAll status-deciding conditions and detail extractions now grep `$log` — the file the\nharness already wrote — instead of piping `$out`. No producer to kill, and the row and\nthe log come from ONE source so they cannot disagree. Verified: corpus run locally\nunder CI's exact env = 382 (same as without tier tracing) and **0 of 1090 rows\ndisagree with their own log**.\n\n- Every CI conformance number taken while tier tracing was on was DEFLATED by an\n  unknown amount. 406→405 was not a regression; those 3 cases passed.\n- Strongly suspect this is [[bugs_conformance_crash_timeout_bimodality_in_ci]] —\n  a timing-dependent misclassification that fires more under load has exactly that\n  shape. Re-check that entry against post-63f45661 runs before trusting its model.\n- Possibly a contributor to [[bugs_conformance_bistable_mode_cluster]] (mac-vs-CI\n  gap). The mac numbers were NOT affected (no tier trace locally), so the ~41-case\n  cluster still needs its own explanation, but any CI-side member of it is suspect.\n\nNever use `producer | early-exiting-consumer` as a CONDITION under `pipefail`\n(`grep -q`, `grep -m1`, `head -n`). Read from a file, or use a here-string.\nCommand substitutions are safe — the status is discarded and the output was already\ncaptured.\n\n- Index summary moved from MEMORY.md (2026-10-18): FIXED 63f45661: `printf|grep -q` under pipefail returned 141 when grep matched EARLY ⇒ PASSING cases scored NO_OUTPUT, CI-only. ALL past CI conformance numbers were DEFLATED. Prime suspect for the CI bimodality.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_conformance_pipefail_sigpipe_misscore` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}